{"data":{"id":28321,"name":"Polygon (prev. MATIC)","symbol":"POL","slug":"polygon-ecosystem-token","category":"token","description":"### What is POL (prev. MATIC)?\nPOL (prev. MATIC) is a cryptocurrency that plays a pivotal role in the blockchain ecosystem, particularly within the Polygon network. Polygon (PoS) is a Proof-of-Stake scaling solution for Ethereum, and the default choice for sending money onchain. POL serves as the native gas token of this ecosystem, powering all transactions, and staking token, securing the network. \n\nIn return for staking, stakers earn rewards, incentivizing network security and participation. They can also become eligible for Agglayer ecosystem airdrops. \n\n### What are the real-world applications of POL (prev. MATIC)?\nPOL (prev. MATIC) is a cryptocurrency that plays a vital role in the Polygon ecosystem, a platform designed to enhance the scalability and usability of Ethereum and power global financial transaction. \n\nA significant application of POL is in the realm of payments and tokenized assets. Businesses and individuals can use POL to make seamless payments, benefiting from its efficiency and low transaction costs. Additionally, POL supports the creation and management of tokenized assets, enabling users to issue and trade digital assets on the Polygon network. This capability is crucial for industries looking to leverage blockchain technology for asset management and transfer.\n\nIn the context of decentralized finance (DeFi), POL is used to power various financial services, such as lending, borrowing, and trading, across the Polygon network. These services benefit from the scalability and low transaction costs that POL provides, making DeFi more accessible to a broader audience.\n\n### What key events have there been for POL (prev. MATIC)?\nOriginally known as MATIC, the token was integral to the Polygon network, which aimed to address Ethereum's scalability issues. This initiative was crucial in enhancing transaction speeds and reducing costs, making it a popular choice for developers and users seeking efficient blockchain interactions.\n\nA significant transformation occurred with the upgrade from MATIC to POL, marking a new era for the Polygon ecosystem. This transition was not merely a rebranding but a strategic move to align with the network's expanded capabilities and revamped GigaGas roadmap to power a chain built for real-world scale and real-time utility. The migration from MATIC to POL officially happened September 4th, 2024.\n\nIn addition to the technical upgrade, the Polygon network has been proactive in fostering a vibrant community of developers and users. This community-driven approach has been instrumental in driving adoption and innovation within the ecosystem. As the network continues to expand its capabilities and reach, POL is poised to play a significant role in shaping the future of decentralized finance and blockchain applications on Polygon.","dateAdded":"2023-10-30T14:43:57.000Z","actualTimeStart":"2023-10-25T12:10:00.000Z","status":"active","isBn":1,"notice":"","alertLink":"","latestUpdateTime":"2026-10-19T06:44:00.000Z","watchCount":"179271","watchListRanking":242,"dateLaunched":"2023-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","latestAdded":false,"launchPrice":0.00263,"tags":[{"slug":"ethereum-ecosystem","name":"Ethereum Ecosystem","category":"PLATFORM","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"layer-2","name":"Layer 2","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"polygon-ecosystem","name":"Polygon Ecosystem","category":"PLATFORM","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"binance-ecosystem","name":"Binance Ecosystem","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"binance-listing","name":"Binance Listing","category":"CATEGORY","status":0,"priority":5}],"selfReportedTags":["PoS","Payments","Staking","Ethereum Ecosystem","Software","Layer 2","Polygon Ecosystem","Web3","Opensource","Polygon Ventures Portfolio"],"selfReportedCirculatingSupply":"10496230782.91","urls":{"websit